<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Edward, Duke of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1884">1884</a>–<a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Edward, Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a>, was a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a>, born Duke of Albany in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, who inherited the German duchy in 1900. He fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, was stripped of his British titles and abdicated in November 1918. He later became a prominent supporter of the Nazi regime.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-edward-duke-of-saxe-coburg-and-gotha.jpg" alt="Charles Edward, Duke of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-2007-0184,_Karl-Eduard_von_Sachsen-Coburg_und_Gotha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
